solution:
**Given:**

x - 2y = 3

**Concept used: **

A system of equation has infinitely many solutions, if the below is satisfied;

dfrac{A₁}{A₂} = dfrac{B₁}{B₂} = dfrac{C₁}{C₂} 

**Calculation:**

Option 1:

⇒ dfrac{1}{2} = dfrac{-2}{-4} ne dfrac{3}{9} 

Option 2:

⇒ dfrac{1}{4} = dfrac{-2}{-8} = dfrac{3}{12} 

**∴ 4x - 8y = 12 will form a system of equations with x - 2y = 3 that has infinitely many solutions.**
